<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Citânia de Briteiros</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Citânia de Briteiros is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guimaraes">Guimarães</a> in northern Portugal, one of the largest settlements of the castro culture of the Callaeci. It had paved streets, round stone houses, defensive walls and a bathhouse with a carved stone slab, the Pedra Formosa. Excavated from 1875 by Francisco Martins Sarmento, it was occupied into the Roman period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/citania-de-briteiros.jpg" alt="Citânia de Briteiros" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TarichaRivularis · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cit%C3%A2nia_de_Briteiros_houses_and_paving.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
